.TH ACC-DEPLOY 1 2026-10-22 "ACC" "ACC Manual"
.SH NAME
acc-deploy \- build, start, stop and reconcile the ACC container stack
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B acc-deploy
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B acc-deploy
drives the ACC stack on a host with
.BR podman-compose (1):
NATS, Redis, one container per agent, the TUI, and optionally the web UI.
It picks the compose files, resolves the image version and the host
layout, and runs the requested command, so callers never need to remember
file paths.
Without a command it runs \fBup\fR.
.PP
On an RPM install the
.B acc-stack.service
unit runs \fBacc\-deploy up \-\-webgui\fR as the unprivileged \fBacc\fR
user with rootless podman, and \fBacc\-deploy down\fR to stop.
.BR acc (1)
runs it as \fBacc stack\fR.
It is part of the \fBacc\fR package only: a container that installs
\fBacc\-runtime\fR has no stack to drive.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Lifecycle
.TP
.BR up " [" \-\-webgui ]
Start the stack, detached (the default command).
\fB\-\-webgui\fR adds the web UI.
.TP
.BR down " [" \-v ]
Stop and remove the containers; \fB\-v\fR also removes the volumes.
.TP
.B restart
Roll the stack onto the current images (down, then up with
force-recreate).
Use it after \fBbuild\fR or \fBrebuild\fR: a plain restart reuses the old
image.
.TP
.BR status ", " ps
Show the running ACC containers.
.TP
.BR logs " [" \fIservice\fR ]
Tail the logs of every service, or of one.
\fBlogs acc\-tui\fR reads the TUI's log file from its volume, since the
TUI's standard output is screen drawing, not log text.
.TP
.B tui\-logs
The same as \fBlogs acc\-tui\fR.
.TP
.BR version ", " image ", " images
Print the resolved code version and whether each image for it is built.
.SS Images
.TP
.B build
Build the container images; needed before the first \fBup\fR.
.TP
.B rebuild
Pull the checkout fast-forward, then rebuild every image with no cache and
fresh base images.
It does not restart the stack: run \fBrestart\fR afterwards.
.TP
.BI "flavour " name " " \fR[ options ]
Build an immutable flavour image: a base with chosen packs baked in and the
governance and control roles always included.
Options: \fB\-\-profile\fR \fIP\fR or \fB\-\-features\fR "\fIa b\fR",
\fB\-\-packs\fR "\fIpacks\fR", \fB\-\-local\-catalog\fR (an unsigned
development bake) or \fB\-\-signer\-key\fR \fIpubkey\fR (verify signed packs
at build), \fB\-\-base\fR \fIimage\fR, \fB\-\-registry\fR \fIR\fR,
\fB\-\-push\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR.
Profiles: \fBnano\fR, \fBstandard\fR, \fBvoice\fR, \fBedge\fR; bundles:
\fBcomms\fR, \fBoffice\fR; \fBfulltest\fR.
.TP
.BI "new\-stack " name " \-\-packs " packs " " \fR[ options ]
Roll a dedicated stack: write \fIcollective.<name>.yaml\fR (control set and
domain agents) and build, tag and optionally push a flavour with its roles
baked in.
Options: \fB\-\-agents\fR \fIr1,r2\fR, \fB\-\-profile\fR
{\fBfull\fR|\fBedge\fR|\fBedge\-min\fR|\fBdc\fR}, \fB\-\-registry\fR
\fIR\fR, \fB\-\-push\fR.
.SS Agentsets
.TP
.BR apply " [" \fIspec\fR "] [" \-\-dry\-run "] [" \-\-prune "] [" \-\-recreate ]
Reconcile the running agents with \fIcollective.yaml\fR, or with
\fIspec\fR: a path, or a preset name under \fIcollectives/\fR
(\fBapply coding\-split\fR reads \fIcollectives/collective.coding\-split.yaml\fR).
Additive and non-disruptive by default: agents in the spec that are not
running are started; the TUI and the baseline keep running.
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the diff; \fB\-\-prune\fR also removes agents not
in the spec; \fB\-\-recreate\fR applies configuration changes to running
agents, restarting them.
.TP
.BR instance " {" up | down | synth "} " \fIid\fR
Run, stop, or render the compose overlay of an instance: a collective bound
to an owner, a posture and its own state roots (see
\fBacc\-cli instance\fR).
.TP
.BI "hibernate " cid
Stop a sub-collective's containers and keep its volumes, so its memory
survives.
.TP
.BI "resume " cid
Bring a hibernated sub-collective back.
.SS Workspaces
.TP
.BI "apply\-workspace " path
Point the agents' \fI/workspace\fR mount at \fIpath\fR and recreate only the
agents; the TUI and the memory volumes are untouched.
The path must lie under \fBACC_WORKSPACE_BASE\fR (default: the deploying
user's home).
.TP
.BR watcher " {" start | stop | status }
The host-side watcher that runs \fBapply\-workspace\fR when the TUI asks.
.TP
.BR lifecycle\-watcher " {" start | stop | status }
The host-side watcher that runs \fBhibernate\fR and \fBresume\fR when the
collective asks.
.SS Other
.TP
.B setup
Create \fI.env\fR from \fI.env.example\fR when it is absent.
.TP
.BI "pkg " verb " " \fR[ args ]
Run
.BR acc-pkg (1)
against the stack's packages root.
\fBpkg add\fR \fI@scope/name\fR [\fIcatalog\fR] fetches and installs by
name; \fBpkg list\fR [\fB\-\-available\fR]; \fBpkg install\fR
\fIfile.accpkg\fR; \fBinspect\fR, \fBeval\fR, \fBverify\fR, \fBinfo\fR and
\fBcontents\fR pass through.
.TP
.BI "cli " args...
Run
.BR acc-cli (1)
once in its container, with host networking and the configuration and
roles mounted read-only.
.TP
.I other
Any other command is passed to \fBpodman\-compose\fR with the selected
compose files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.BR ACC_HOME ", " ACC_SHARE ", " ACC_STATE
The configuration, the data trees (\fIcontainer/\fR, \fIroles/\fR) and the
state; unset, all three are the directory of the script, as in a checkout.
.TP
.B ACC_ENV_FILE
The secrets file (default \fI$ACC_HOME/.env\fR; the RPM uses
\fI/etc/acc/acc.env\fR).
.TP
.B ACC_VERSION
The image tag to build and run (default: \fBgit describe\fR of the
checkout, else the installed package version).
.TP
.B ACC_IMAGE_PREFIX
The image registry prefix (default \fBlocalhost\fR).
.TP
.BR STACK "=" production | beta
Which compose file (default \fBproduction\fR).
.TP
.BR TUI ", " WEBGUI ", " CODING_SPLIT ", " MCP_ECHO ", " AUTORESEARCHER "=" true | false
Include the TUI (default true), the web UI, the coding-split demo agents,
the diagnostic echo MCP server, or the research MCP servers (default false).
.TP
.BR DETACH "=" false
Run in the foreground.
.TP
.BR ACC_SUPPORT_TIER "=" upstream | rhel
Where subscription-gated images (Redis) come from at build time: the
community image (default), or RHEL AppStream on UBI 9, which needs an
entitled build host.
.TP
.BR ACC_CLI_IMAGE ", " ACC_CLI_NETWORK
The image and network of \fBcli\fR.
.TP
.BR ACC_NATS_URL ", " ACC_COLLECTIVE_ID
The bus and default collective for \fBcli\fR.
.TP
.B ACC_ALLOW_UNSIGNED
Set to 1 to let \fBpkg\fR install unsigned development packs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/acc/acc\-deploy.sh
The script itself (\fI/usr/bin/acc\-deploy\fR links to it).
.TP
.I /usr/share/acc/container/production
The compose files and Containerfiles.
.TP
.I /etc/acc/acc.env
The stack's secrets on an RPM install.
.TP
.I /usr/lib/systemd/system/acc\-stack.service
The unit that runs the stack as the \fBacc\fR user.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
acc\-deploy build && acc\-deploy up \-\-webgui
acc\-deploy apply \-\-dry\-run
acc\-deploy logs acc\-agent\-ingester
acc\-deploy cli oversight pending
TUI=false acc\-deploy up
systemctl status acc\-stack
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR acc (1),
.BR acc-cli (1),
.BR acc-pkg (1),
.BR podman-compose (1),
.BR systemctl (1)
